      "side": 1,
      "message": "These are just loose comments, mostly trying to point out the various issues.\n\nThis isn\u0027t even mentioning the fact bpf offloads make this code not even trigger events at the right times... which simply cannot be fixed with this iptables based approach, because iptables simply doesn\u0027t even see such packets.\n\nAlso as you know, we basically have no test coverage for this, and we\u0027d need to backport this to all the other ACK branches... and wait for months and months for devices to actually pick it up.\n\nIf we\u0027re going to go to the effort of fixing something, and then cherrypicking ahoying, and testing... we should try to fix more than just this one nit.",
